    {
      "id": "claim_8473cd6c69af4cc59175cf44f9f11fc2",
      "statement": "The Bucket keeps a separate conditional-write store built with retries off, because a retried CAS put can land on the first attempt's own token change and report a clean 412, converting may-have-committed into a false rejection.",
